WEBVTT

00:01.030 --> 00:05.000
I jumped into this world of my own free will,

00:05.000 --> 00:09.300
but at the same time, it was also because
Amir Gaul was beckoning me.

00:09.300 --> 00:15.270
If the key spirits are causing the wars,
then I'll stop those wars.

00:28.620 --> 00:36.230
Umareta machi o tooku hanarete atashi wa

00:36.230 --> 00:39.400
Utatte iru

00:39.400 --> 00:47.040
Yowai kokoro mo yureru omoi mo poketto ni

00:47.040 --> 00:50.310
Shimaikonde

00:50.310 --> 01:00.890
Te no naru hou e michi naru michi e

01:00.890 --> 01:06.330
Ayumou

01:06.330 --> 01:11.730
Susumou

01:11.730 --> 01:16.570
Dare ka no tame ja naku

01:16.570 --> 01:22.040
Aru ga mama hokoreru you ni

01:22.040 --> 01:27.520
Yoake ni taiyou ga noboru you ni

01:27.520 --> 01:32.750
Atashi wa melody o kizamu

01:32.750 --> 01:36.780
Hakanakutomo tsuyoku

01:38.430 --> 01:41.950
Atashi wa ikite yuku

01:46.870 --> 01:50.530
Episode 46
To the Land Where the Decision Will Be made

01:56.310 --> 01:57.940
Zed!

02:01.420 --> 02:03.040
Sagiri...

02:04.420 --> 02:06.420
You're going to Tusk?

02:06.420 --> 02:07.720
Yeah...

02:07.720 --> 02:11.730
To get back the key spirits Xeem stole.

02:11.730 --> 02:14.860
Are you going to get all the key spirits
and become the savior?

02:14.860 --> 02:16.800
Savior?

02:16.800 --> 02:19.430
No, I'm not.

02:20.170 --> 02:24.770
I just want to stop this pointless fighting.

02:24.770 --> 02:27.310
And I sense it...

02:27.310 --> 02:30.440
I think Amir Gaul feels the same way.

02:31.980 --> 02:34.110
He feels the same way?

02:35.150 --> 02:37.120
I kind of feel like he wants to stop

02:37.120 --> 02:41.190
this endless stealing and re-stealing
of the key spirits.

02:41.190 --> 02:45.490
That must be why he chose me.

02:51.830 --> 02:54.670
You can have this!

02:54.670 --> 02:55.970
That's your...

02:55.970 --> 02:57.070
It's okay!

02:57.070 --> 03:00.040
I don't want to be the savior either,

03:00.040 --> 03:02.310
and I don't want any power!

03:02.310 --> 03:04.110
So, in return...

03:04.910 --> 03:07.880
In return, find Noah!

03:08.350 --> 03:09.980
You...

03:10.350 --> 03:14.390
He believed in Absolute Law so much,
and now it's gone.

03:14.390 --> 03:18.890
Noah might be out there suffering right now.

03:18.890 --> 03:21.520
He might be crying all alone!

03:23.870 --> 03:27.320
Please, find Noah.

03:28.200 --> 03:30.000
Protect him!

03:32.440 --> 03:34.240
Don't you worry.

03:36.240 --> 03:39.040
You just leave Noah to me.

03:41.150 --> 03:42.780
Okay!

03:53.030 --> 03:59.570
All we can do for you is to shift you
to the floating continent of Tusk.

03:59.570 --> 04:02.700
I do not know what lies ahead for you there.

04:02.700 --> 04:04.010
That's enough.

04:04.010 --> 04:06.630
I'll manage things from there out.

04:12.280 --> 04:14.410
See you later.

04:22.990 --> 04:24.390
Lord Dolga?

04:24.390 --> 04:27.930
Yes, he will aid us.

04:27.930 --> 04:29.200
Where is he from?

04:29.200 --> 04:31.470
Elmeida brought him here for me.

04:31.470 --> 04:34.200
And can we trust such a man?

04:34.200 --> 04:35.540
What a silly question.

04:35.540 --> 04:36.770
What?!

04:36.770 --> 04:41.730
What's important is that this man has a key spirit.

04:43.340 --> 04:48.580
And he is a believer in the Tuskan ideal
of conquering this world

04:48.580 --> 04:51.590
through Great Tusker's power.

04:51.590 --> 04:53.050
Be that as it may!

04:53.050 --> 04:57.330
I wish for the advent of Great Tusker,

04:57.330 --> 05:00.120
and pledge my loyalty to Tusk.

05:07.600 --> 05:09.230
Molima!

05:10.310 --> 05:12.270
I think it's fine.

05:13.140 --> 05:15.610
He seems interesting.

05:15.610 --> 05:18.080
I welcome him.

05:21.980 --> 05:26.940
I'll have you prove your worthiness
to serve Great Tusker.

05:28.420 --> 05:30.720
Until then, I will not acknowledge you!

05:32.290 --> 05:34.700
A foolish man.

05:34.700 --> 05:36.000
What about the other one?

05:36.000 --> 05:39.960
Gitra hasn't yet returned from the
search for Lady Mirred.

05:41.400 --> 05:45.040
I ask you to help in that search as well.

05:45.040 --> 05:47.170
All right.

05:56.580 --> 05:57.650
Where are we?

05:57.650 --> 05:59.620
This is where I come to get away.

06:03.990 --> 06:05.790
It's wonderful!

06:06.530 --> 06:09.330
There really are gods, aren't there?

06:10.260 --> 06:15.730
I mean, no one but a god could create
something so beautiful!

06:24.110 --> 06:25.650
Say, what is this?

06:25.650 --> 06:27.610
A fossilized spirit.

06:28.520 --> 06:29.780
This too?

06:29.780 --> 06:32.520
That's a fossilized spell shard.

06:32.520 --> 06:34.820
Why are you collecting them?

06:38.990 --> 06:41.200
I want to know the truth.

06:41.200 --> 06:43.230
The truth?

06:43.230 --> 06:48.740
Everyone believes without question that
Tusker created all the shards,

06:48.740 --> 06:50.860
but is that really true?

06:52.340 --> 06:55.470
Did Tusker really have such power?

06:57.180 --> 07:00.980
Well, I don't mean to deny Tusker's power...

07:01.620 --> 07:03.450
It's a good question.

07:03.450 --> 07:06.080
I wonder what Tusker really is?

07:07.260 --> 07:12.560
I wonder why I was born with a key spirit?

07:15.400 --> 07:20.530
So you see, I can understand
how you feel very well.

07:28.510 --> 07:31.640
I can't very well hide her here forever.

07:32.980 --> 07:34.610
But...

07:38.020 --> 07:42.820
What can I do to give her freedom?

09:14.750 --> 09:17.150
I want to see him,

09:17.150 --> 09:21.450
just once more before I return to the castle.

09:26.030 --> 09:30.330
I'm sure if I go to the Cave of Toste...

09:39.710 --> 09:41.780
Okay, you're fine now.

09:41.780 --> 09:43.910
Thank you very much.

09:43.910 --> 09:45.710
Take care.

09:54.890 --> 09:58.520
You're fine, right, Zed?

10:05.900 --> 10:07.530
Tusk...

10:12.240 --> 10:14.710
Just you wait, Xeem!

10:17.380 --> 10:19.750
You still can't find her?!

10:19.750 --> 10:21.520
I trust you realize that if something
happens to Lady Mirred,

10:21.520 --> 10:24.850
our ideals will be completely shattered!

10:24.850 --> 10:26.620
Find her, on the double!

10:26.620 --> 10:28.250
Yes, sir!

10:29.020 --> 10:31.650
I wonder if that's really the case?

10:32.390 --> 10:35.660
Molima, what are you doing?!

10:35.660 --> 10:38.770
Are your men searching seriously?!

10:38.770 --> 10:41.060
Of course they are.

10:42.600 --> 10:45.540
What is it you're thinking?

10:45.540 --> 10:49.940
I'm just faithfully doing my duty for
the resurrection of Great Tusker,

10:49.940 --> 10:52.070
just like you.

10:52.780 --> 10:54.820
Oh, that's right.

10:54.820 --> 10:57.780
Are you familiar with Gitra's hideout?

11:04.130 --> 11:05.750
Gitra...

11:07.530 --> 11:09.760
I'm going back to the castle.

11:09.760 --> 11:11.400
Lady Mirred!

11:11.400 --> 11:14.940
I'm sure Xeem and the others are
searching for me right now.

11:14.940 --> 11:18.740
It will cause trouble for you too
if I stay here too long.

11:19.210 --> 11:20.310
Don't say that!

11:20.310 --> 11:23.110
A chance like this may never come again!

11:24.750 --> 11:28.550
I'm smart enough to have known
all along that I can't get away.

11:29.850 --> 11:37.090
But there is one favor I'd like to ask
before I return to the castle.

11:37.090 --> 11:38.890
What is it?

11:39.430 --> 11:42.400
Take me to the Cave of Toste one more time!

11:43.730 --> 11:46.030
To the Cave of Toste?

11:55.940 --> 11:57.740
Hey, over here!

11:58.180 --> 11:59.880
Call Captain Miguel right away!

11:59.880 --> 12:01.050
Secure the perimeter!

12:01.050 --> 12:02.050
Right!

12:02.050 --> 12:03.380
Hurry, they're this way!

12:03.380 --> 12:05.350
Don't let them get away!

12:13.260 --> 12:15.800
Please flee out the back way.

12:15.800 --> 12:19.100
You can't let them dictate your life anymore.

12:19.100 --> 12:19.770
But...

12:19.770 --> 12:21.230
Hurry!
But...

12:34.680 --> 12:38.390
A witness reports seeing Lady Mirred here.

12:38.390 --> 12:41.010
I trust you'll hand her over?

12:43.260 --> 12:45.730
Lady Mirred can't have gotten far.

12:46.790 --> 12:47.290
Find her.

12:47.290 --> 12:48.300
Yes, sir!
Find her.

12:48.300 --> 12:50.260
I won't let that happen!

12:51.830 --> 12:53.630
Get him!

13:02.580 --> 13:04.200
Gitra!

13:12.450 --> 13:14.250
I want to see him...

13:14.660 --> 13:17.280
I want to see him one more time.

13:19.930 --> 13:21.560
The wench sure caused us trouble!

13:21.560 --> 13:23.860
All right, let's take her back.

13:25.430 --> 13:27.230
What was that?

13:32.010 --> 13:33.800
Hey, are you okay?

13:34.640 --> 13:36.940
Pull yourself together! Hey!

13:39.080 --> 13:40.580
What is it?

13:40.580 --> 13:43.210
Have to get there...

13:52.630 --> 13:54.420
Lady Mirred!

13:59.530 --> 14:00.900
What should I do?

14:00.900 --> 14:04.310
I want to book it on over to the castle,

14:04.310 --> 14:07.430
but I can't just leave her like this.

14:13.750 --> 14:16.780
You guys just keep coming, don't you?
Give it a rest!

14:16.780 --> 14:18.220
You bastard...

14:18.220 --> 14:20.520
What have you done to Lady Mirred?!

14:24.760 --> 14:26.390
Gitra...

14:26.790 --> 14:28.590
Stop, Gitra!

14:30.430 --> 14:34.370
That man helped me!

14:34.370 --> 14:35.940
He did?

14:35.940 --> 14:39.060
Oh, you're a friend of hers?

14:41.380 --> 14:42.640
So, that's how it is.

14:42.640 --> 14:44.080
I'm sorry.

14:44.080 --> 14:46.050
Nah, I understand.

14:46.050 --> 14:48.950
But what are you doing out here?

14:48.950 --> 14:50.850
I want to go to the castle.

14:50.850 --> 14:52.650
The castle?!

14:57.220 --> 15:01.020
My my, I didn't think I'd get to see you here.

15:01.230 --> 15:03.200
You're Dukeham!

15:03.200 --> 15:08.500
Gitra, you'll be telling me all about your little
escapade with Lady Mirred later.

15:09.900 --> 15:11.870
I'll deal with you first.

15:12.340 --> 15:14.140
Amir Gaul!

15:17.340 --> 15:19.140
Let's go!

15:19.610 --> 15:23.070
I'll purge the humiliation I suffered
in Ulvarx here and now!

15:29.990 --> 15:32.060
That's Amir Gaul!

15:32.060 --> 15:34.360
Then, he's Zed?!

15:38.400 --> 15:41.860
I will kill you here and take Amir Gaul!

15:43.200 --> 15:44.510
You too, huh?

15:44.510 --> 15:46.130
What?

15:48.810 --> 15:52.110
You're all freaking obsessed with the key spirits!

15:54.480 --> 15:57.320
And because you won't stop
your fighting over them,

15:57.320 --> 15:59.250
lots of people keep dying!

15:59.250 --> 16:04.060
Naturally, some sacrifices must be made
for the prosperity of Tusk!

16:04.060 --> 16:06.690
It's to gain the key spirits!

16:07.960 --> 16:13.090
I'll be the one to get all the key spirits!

16:17.740 --> 16:20.710
And then I'll stop all the fighting!

16:20.710 --> 16:24.170
What? Do you mean to become the savior?!

16:25.050 --> 16:27.340
Him, become the savior?

16:28.650 --> 16:30.450
Amir Gaul!

16:44.060 --> 16:45.860
I can't believe this guy.

16:46.170 --> 16:47.960
Doom Blitz!

16:53.070 --> 16:54.870
Amir Gaul!

16:55.580 --> 16:59.350
You're as good as I'd expect of someone
who caught my eye.

16:59.350 --> 17:01.810
I'll give you credit for your ambitions.

17:02.580 --> 17:04.210
However...

17:09.020 --> 17:12.160
All the key spirits belong to Tusk.

17:12.160 --> 17:15.760
Tusk's savior will be the one to
receive their power.

17:15.760 --> 17:17.560
Not you!

17:18.470 --> 17:21.540
I've got no intention of being a savior.

17:21.540 --> 17:23.160
What?!

17:25.540 --> 17:29.210
You people are so blined by greed
for the key spirits' power

17:29.210 --> 17:32.180
that you won't stop warring!

17:34.050 --> 17:36.520
I just can't forgive you!

18:07.010 --> 18:08.880
There's no way...

18:08.880 --> 18:14.840
There's no way I'd lose to a little brat like you!

18:31.210 --> 18:33.410
Thank you for saving me.

18:33.410 --> 18:36.540
Sure, it's no big deal.

18:39.810 --> 18:41.280
The name is Gitra.

18:41.280 --> 18:43.280
I'm one of Tusk's high officials.

18:43.280 --> 18:45.120
You are?

18:45.120 --> 18:47.190
Are you Zed?

18:47.190 --> 18:48.620
Yeah...

18:48.620 --> 18:53.750
Zed, do you seriously intend to
gather all the key spirits?

18:58.370 --> 19:02.500
Lady Mirred, would you mind hiding here
and waiting for a little while?

19:02.500 --> 19:04.000
Why?

19:04.000 --> 19:06.440
I'm going to lead Zed to the castle.

19:06.440 --> 19:09.240
Huh? What's the deal here?!

19:09.240 --> 19:11.040
Come with me.

19:22.290 --> 19:24.320
What's your agenda?

19:24.320 --> 19:28.600
Why would a Tuskan official
lead me to the castle?

19:28.600 --> 19:32.550
Because you said you seriously mean
to gather all the key spirits.

19:34.470 --> 19:39.410
In Tusk, it's said that the one who can wield
all the key spirits is the savior,

19:39.410 --> 19:42.200
and can gain Tusker's power.

19:43.080 --> 19:48.180
And it's believed that the one who will
become the savior is Lady Mirred,

19:48.180 --> 19:50.080
who was born with a key spirit.

19:50.080 --> 19:51.590
Mirred...

19:51.590 --> 19:53.380
Her, huh?

19:58.090 --> 20:00.530
Because of that fate, Lady Mirred has
been a sacrificial victim here

20:00.530 --> 20:03.330
all her life up till now.

20:04.700 --> 20:08.600
But if you can gather all the key spirits,

20:08.600 --> 20:11.070
Lady Mirred can be free.

20:14.540 --> 20:15.740
What are those?

20:15.740 --> 20:17.380
Moving shards.

20:17.380 --> 20:19.680
With these, you can get to the castle.

20:21.880 --> 20:25.180
Zed, I want to try entrusting my wishes to you...

20:25.590 --> 20:30.720
...you who have been chosen by Amir Gaul.

20:36.500 --> 20:40.800
The castle guard is understaffed right now
because of the search for Lady Mirred.

20:42.670 --> 20:45.140
When you get up there, run as fast as you can.

20:45.770 --> 20:48.400
When you enter the first tower, turn left.

20:54.110 --> 20:57.570
On the other side of the third tower is
the entrance to a secret passage.

20:57.920 --> 21:00.220
It's marked by a fossilized spirit.

21:02.220 --> 21:05.190
If you get through the passage,
you'll be inside the castle.

21:08.430 --> 21:10.560
Where's Xeem?

21:28.220 --> 21:31.650
Damn it! It's practically a maze!

21:31.650 --> 21:33.620
What should I do now?

21:34.620 --> 21:36.490
What?!

21:36.490 --> 21:39.160
You still can't pick up Mirred's trail?!

21:39.160 --> 21:41.630
Expand the scope of the search!

22:01.010 --> 22:02.640
You're...

22:13.330 --> 22:15.260
Dolga...

22:15.260 --> 22:16.660
Who the hell are you?

22:16.660 --> 22:18.630
Don't get in my way!

22:24.910 --> 22:26.870
That spirit...

22:28.080 --> 22:30.540
Don't tell me you're...

22:39.620 --> 22:44.920
Wazurawashii toko kara hanarete

22:45.860 --> 22:49.230
Habatakitakatta dake

22:49.230 --> 22:54.430
Mou kodomo ja nai no ni to

22:54.430 --> 23:00.070
Nando jibun o shikatta darou

23:01.140 --> 23:05.980
Yakusoku sareta basho made

23:05.980 --> 23:11.620
Hitasura susumu dake sa

23:11.620 --> 23:17.220
Bokura no tsubasa wa

23:17.220 --> 23:24.000
Honmono no totemo totemo kirei na hane dakara

23:24.000 --> 23:33.740
Donna hageshii ooki na kaze ni mo makenai

23:33.740 --> 23:43.820
Tooku e tooku e hitasura tobun da

23:43.820 --> 23:49.560
Hora mou kaze ni natte

23:49.560 --> 23:57.930
Anna ni namida o koraeta hi mo waraeru kara

23:59.930 --> 24:03.890
Sekai no hate made

24:17.720 --> 24:20.940
Next Time
A Savior Adrift

24:17.950 --> 24:20.940


Next Time, "A Savior Adrift"
